  "selected": [
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "The whole comparison must be done on one shared mask (WOA23 landsea_01, >1 = ocean) applied to every field, and the model ranking is only meaningful on the cells all models and WOA23 share.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Regrid all three models to the WOA23 1° grid, build one mask over all fields with `build_comparison_mask` (keep its default `ocean_only=True`, since WOA23 is the reference here), apply it with `.where(mask)` to every field before bias, RMSE and correlation, and report the mask's cell count.",
        "Quote `mean_data` and `mean_reference` from `compute_difference_metrics` over that shared sample next to each `delta_SST`; a model's own-grid global mean is a different quantity and is not the comparison mean."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "The native global means for each model require area weighting by areacello over the ocean cells, and the WOA23 global mean over the 1-degree grid requires its own cell-area weighting rather than a plain cell average.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Global mean per model: Σ tos·areacello / Σ areacello over valid ocean cells with NaN-aware weights — never an unweighted mean over (y, x) on a curvilinear grid or over latitude on a regular one.",
        "RMSE and the Pearson correlation must be area-weighted (`compute_difference_metrics` weights by area by default; `analyze_correlation` needs `weighting='area'`); the WOA23 \"whole 1-degree grid\" mean is area-weighted only if so computed — state which was taken, since the two differ."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-static-grid-fields",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-static-grid-fields.md",
      "sha256": "2ad0548ca0993fa57d8f1fad27a267dcf9c0e1d007a74343d4bbdbf5b4f1ca17",
      "reason": "Defines areacello as tracer-cell horizontal area, which is the weight to use for the native-grid global means and for any area-weighted statistic.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Use each model's published `areacello` as the only correct area weight on its curvilinear grid, and state the total ocean area each mean covers; total areas differ by about a per cent between models and are not to be rescaled."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-tos-bulk-top-cell",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-tos-bulk-top-cell.md",
      "sha256": "4acdeba0f49784d4435dbc4eed34ca9777254313daa951641759fa02df24cf64",
      "reason": "tos is the top-cell bulk temperature, not a skin temperature, and top-cell thickness differs by model, which must be stated when its 1971-2000 climatology is compared with WOA23's 0 m analysis.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`tos` is the bulk temperature of the top cell including under sea ice, so polar values near −1.8 °C are data, not missing, and enter a global mean; make the model and WOA23 ocean masks consistent where the observation masks sea ice before comparing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "missing-values-and-land-cells",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "pitfalls/missing-values-and-land-cells.md",
      "sha256": "f576244f13dde06fed1777eaa9721c68844f61758f66fac704b44f1551e90df2",
      "reason": "CMIP6 land and below-sea-floor cells are 1e20 missing values, so the read path must apply CF masking before any mean or bias is computed or the sums will be dominated by huge numbers.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Build each field's valid mask from the field itself (valid cells differ between variables), mask the weights to the same cells, and treat any value near 1e20 as an unmasked fill value."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-native-grid-vs-regridded",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-native-grid-vs-regridded.md",
      "sha256": "8ff046ffbadc5794fcd2f8fe93d3bb947c736dec650aa3a3cd6e2412b7da8e68",
      "reason": "Integrals and native means must be computed on each model's own grid with its own areas, and regridding to the WOA23 1-degree grid is only for the maps and the cell-by-cell comparison, since it changes masks and breaks conservation.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compute the four global means on each source's own grid with its own `areacello`; regrid only for the maps, bias, RMSE and pattern correlation on the common mask, and state the method ('conservative' when going to the coarser 1° grid), because the regridded metrics depend on it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-grid-labels",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "datasets/cmip6-grid-labels.md",
      "sha256": "e349f9e305621b6c10b35cccd0490da521cc7e3ba08bfb53890479f81024d117",
      "reason": "CESM2 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are gn (curvilinear native) whereas GFDL-ESM4 is gr (already conservatively regridded to 1°×1°, 35 z levels), which affects masks, which operations are exact and how the native-grid means are formed.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "GFDL-ESM4 carries `gr`: its \"native-grid\" numbers are on its 1° regridded archive grid with a regridded land–sea mask, and resolution differs (CESM2 ~100 km vs MPI ~250 km), so narrow features are not comparable in amplitude."
      ]
    },
